# Build context for runner/Dockerfile is the repo root (it compiles the
# pillbox binary in-image). Keep the context small: Cargo.* + src/ +
# runner/entrypoint.sh and runner/install-codex-package.sh are COPYed, so
# exclude the heavy/irrelevant dirs but keep those two files (excluding all of
# runner/ broke the build because the Dockerfile COPYs them).
target/
.git/
.github/
docs/
tests/
runner/*
!runner/entrypoint.sh
!runner/install-codex-package.sh
.claude/
*.md
.env*
# The vendored rustic_backend manifest names its README and licenses. Keep
# those package metadata files in the build context alongside the source.
!vendor/rustic_backend/README.md
!vendor/rustic_backend/LICENSE-APACHE
!vendor/rustic_backend/LICENSE-MIT
